# iOS + Android + Web parity

The consumer product is the Expo Router tree (`app/`, `components/`, `hooks/`, `lib/`). All three platforms run it. Full policy: `AGENTS.md`.

- Do **not** add social / feed / challenge UX to `web/components/blob-app.tsx` or a Next-only UI.
- Default to React Native primitives + `Platform.OS` / feature detection. No separate screens per OS unless required.
- Native-only (Health, push) must keep Web/Android/iOS usable: photo proof, in-app alerts, or an honest empty state — never a dead control.
- Camera / Wave / Round needs a Web path (`getUserMedia` or gallery).
- Auth: `blob://auth/callback` + `blob://oauthredirect` (native) and https `/auth/callback` (Web). Never fix one platform only.
- Chrome: shared `tabBarLift` / `ChromeOverlay` (never RN `Modal` for sheets). Mouse and touch.
- One Supabase project. `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` for EAS and Vercel. Deploy user-facing work on the team branch (e.g. `blob-beta-three`).

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — consumer feature only on the thin web harness
// web/components/blob-app.tsx

// ❌ BAD — Web dead end
if (Platform.OS !== 'ios') return null;

// ✅ GOOD — shared screen, gated native extra
<ProofUploader />
{Platform.OS === 'ios' ? <UseWorkoutChip /> : null}
```

**Done only when** the same primary journey works on iOS, Android, and Web (or a documented fallback), and the implementer states all three.
